1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:01,554
Welcome to FarmTact.

2
00:00:01,554 --> 00:00:07,321
On the left is the desktop workspace; on the right, the same journey on mobile.

3
00:00:07,321 --> 00:00:10,013
We are using an isolated synthetic farm.

4
00:00:10,013 --> 00:00:16,549
Start with the short introduction: inspect a delivery question, compare plans, review changes, and report what happened.

5
00:00:20,433 --> 00:00:25,250
Our starting question is whether the farm can cover a dated order for caixin.

6
00:00:25,250 --> 00:00:27,315
Scroll down to the farm picture.

7
00:00:27,315 --> 00:00:30,756
Recorded crops occupy named beds, while empty beds stay empty.

8
00:00:30,756 --> 00:00:35,573
Cash, labour, and the planning horizon provide the context for a realistic planting decision.

9
00:00:40,467 --> 00:00:44,126
Open the Farm Inbox to see which records are active.

10
00:00:44,126 --> 00:00:47,420
This example uses the labelled Singapore leafy greens fixture.

11
00:00:47,420 --> 00:00:52,178
Uploaded documents and manual entries must be reviewed before they become accepted evidence.

12
00:00:52,178 --> 00:00:56,570
For this walkthrough, we keep the existing records and return to planning.

13
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:01,983
Choose Compare planting plans.

14
00:01:01,983 --> 00:01:07,544
The local numerical engine now checks crop timing and resource constraints against the recorded demand.

15
00:01:07,544 --> 00:01:10,510
This is a real calculation in the app.

16
00:01:10,510 --> 00:01:16,812
When it finishes, the alternatives appear with their own coverage, expiry, and contribution margin, ready for comparison.

17
00:01:25,533 --> 00:01:28,863
We inspect Balanced, then Resilient, and return to Balanced.

18
00:01:28,863 --> 00:01:32,562
Watch the selected candidate and the projected measures change together.

19
00:01:32,562 --> 00:01:38,111
Feasible means the model's constraints hold; it does not promise that every order is filled.

20
00:01:38,111 --> 00:01:41,811
Read the shortfall alongside the margin before making a choice.

21
00:01:45,567 --> 00:01:48,543
Now bring the tradeoff to the Planning Council.

22
00:01:48,543 --> 00:01:50,775
Each specialist has a distinct responsibility.

23
00:01:50,775 --> 00:01:54,867
We type a focused question about booked deliveries and crop timing.

24
00:01:54,867 --> 00:01:59,331
This remains a draft: only pressing Send or Ask Council requests advice.

25
00:01:59,331 --> 00:02:03,423
No generated response is being presented as a completed review here.

26
00:02:10,600 --> 00:02:14,087
Suppose expected demand for caixin rises by five percent.

27
00:02:14,087 --> 00:02:17,574
Open Adjust assumptions and enter one hundred and five.

28
00:02:17,574 --> 00:02:19,899
Read the exact changes before recalculating.

29
00:02:19,899 --> 00:02:27,260
The date range, crop, and capacity remain visible, so we can check precisely what the next calculation will use.

30
00:02:45,200 --> 00:02:47,234
The revised alternatives are ready.

31
00:02:47,234 --> 00:02:51,710
Saving is a separate decision from calculating or asking for advice.

32
00:02:51,710 --> 00:02:55,372
Open Save simulation plan, review its boundary, and confirm.

33
00:02:55,372 --> 00:02:59,847
FarmTact records this approved revision and creates its simulated work list.

34
00:02:59,847 --> 00:03:03,509
It does not operate equipment or contact a buyer.

35
00:03:05,233 --> 00:03:09,692
Move to the work list and open a task from the approved plan.

36
00:03:09,692 --> 00:03:13,465
Its crop, location, planned quantity, and checklist provide the reporting context.

37
00:03:13,465 --> 00:03:15,523
We will demonstrate a short result.

38
00:03:15,523 --> 00:03:21,011
The quantity entered next is an example report, not a measurement collected from a real farm.

39
00:03:25,267 --> 00:03:32,707
Enter a quantity one unit below the task's plan, complete the checklist, and type a clear note explaining the shortage.

40
00:03:32,707 --> 00:03:34,567
Then save the reported result.

41
00:03:34,567 --> 00:03:37,915
Notice that this is labelled farmer reported and unverified.

42
00:03:37,915 --> 00:03:42,380
The short result prompts recovery instead of silently rewriting the original projection.

43
00:03:50,300 --> 00:03:54,285
If a scale reading was wrong, record a correction with a reason.

44
00:03:54,285 --> 00:03:58,601
Here we revise the reported quantity and explain that the scale was checked.

45
00:03:58,601 --> 00:04:01,922
Save auditable correction preserves the history of the first report.

46
00:04:01,922 --> 00:04:05,242
The updated value remains a report, with its provenance intact.

47
00:04:10,333 --> 00:04:12,784
The next decision is Compare recovery plans.

48
00:04:12,784 --> 00:04:17,335
Open it to inspect a future change while keeping completed work in history.

49
00:04:17,335 --> 00:04:21,187
We review the proposal and close it without applying another change.

50
00:04:21,187 --> 00:04:26,088
Recovery is deliberate: opening a form or reading advice does not approve additional work.

51
00:04:30,367 --> 00:04:32,194
For more context, open Crops.

52
00:04:32,194 --> 00:04:36,214
The desktop navigation and mobile menu reach the same knowledge library.

53
00:04:36,214 --> 00:04:40,965
Crop profiles and their evidence help us understand the assumptions behind a plan.

54
00:04:40,965 --> 00:04:47,178
Knowledge is useful context; it should not be confused with a validated prediction for this particular farm.

55
00:04:50,400 --> 00:04:54,051
Back in Plan, How it works opens three short guides.

56
00:04:54,051 --> 00:04:57,701
Each has playback controls, captions, a transcript, and a download.

57
00:04:57,701 --> 00:05:03,542
The introductory demo can also be replayed whenever you want a reminder of the decision sequence.

58
00:05:05,433 --> 00:05:10,890
That is the complete loop: inspect, calculate, question, review, save, and report.

59
00:05:10,890 --> 00:05:19,075
Desktop and mobile preserve the same explicit decisions and the same distinction between projections, simulation, and reported results.
